 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S445-006\", \"clauses\": {\"illustrate_area_with_tiles\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"This {figure} is covered by {rows} rows of {cols} square tiles. How many square tile units cover the {figure}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 asks the learner to picture the tiles covering a figure as rows and columns of square tiles. That is the Illustrate task, and the declared illustrate_tiles task_type renders it.\"}, \"estimate_area\": {\"verdict\": \"NOT_PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": null, \"template\": null, \"reasoning\": \"No family asks for an estimate. F06 asks for the exact count of tiles covering a figure, and F02 and F03 compute an exact product. The declared variants contain no estimate task.\"}, \"area_attribute\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"This {figure} is covered by {rows} rows of {cols} square tiles. How many square tile units cover the {figure}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 asks how many square tile units cover the figure, which is the area of the figure.\"}, \"square_figure\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"This {figure} is covered by {rows} rows of {cols} square tiles. How many square tile units cover the {figure}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 prints figure from the shape domain, whose printed values include square.\"}, \"rectangle_figure\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"This {figure} is covered by {rows} rows of {cols} square tiles. How many square tile units cover the {figure}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 prints figure from the shape domain, whose printed values include rectangle.\"}, \"square_tile_covering\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"This {figure} is covered by {rows} rows of {cols} square tiles. How many square tile units cover the {figure}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 states that the figure is covered by rows of square tiles.\"}, \"square_tile_unit\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"This {figure} is covered by {rows} rows of {cols} square tiles. How many square tile units cover the {figure}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 asks how many square tile units cover the figure, so the tile is the unit of measure.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F02\", \"F03\", \"F06\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Area of a rectangle = length × width = {l} × {w} = {answer} {unit}.\", \"Area of a square = side × side = {s} × {s} = {answer} {unit}.\", \"This {figure} is covered by {rows} rows of {cols} square tiles. How many square tile units cover the {figure}?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F02 and F03 print the unit slot from the domain whose printed value is 'sq cm', a square centimeter. NOT_YET_KNOWN lists 'sq. cm' and 'square centimeter', so the unit is a concept beyond this lc's gate. Both templates also teach an area formula (length × width; side × side) that the competency, which asks for area using square tile units, does not name. F02 also uses 'width', which appears in neither cumulative_vocab nor the packet's vocabulary lists. F06: the rows domain (from s, 2 to 8) and the cols domain (from values['sides'], members 2 to 8) are independent, and the packet shows no rule tying them for shape 'square'. A square can therefore be printed as covered by unequal rows and columns, which is a false statement.\"}",
